<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belz Hasidic dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Belz Hasidism</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belz">Belz</a> Hasidic dynasty is a Hasidic movement founded in the town of Belz in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> by Rabbi Shalom Rokeach, who became its leader in 1817. Under his successors Belz became one of the largest Hasidic courts of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The community was devastated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>, but its leader Aharon Rokeach escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> in 1944, and the movement was rebuilt with its centre in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belz-hasidic-dynasty.jpg" alt="Belz Hasidic dynasty" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belz_hasidic_synagogue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
